 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Swasthi’s card calls for <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tbsp</span> almond meal; the 12 almonds + 8 cashews ground with the yogurt is her own alternative, used here because you remember it with cashews.</li><li><b>Assumed, untested:</b> all cashews — about 20 — should work the same and taste a little sweeter and creamier.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Cashews and almonds"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Swasthi’s malai tikka comes out pale, creamy-white with char spots.</li><li>If the one you remember was yellow, add a pinch of turmeric or a few saffron strands soaked in a teaspoon of warm milk to the marinade.</li><li>That’s an addition, not part of her recipe.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Yellow colour (optional)"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Swasthi notes that restaurants often add cardamom and nutmeg powder (she leaves them out), and that <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> green chilli paste instead of the pepper makes it spicy.</li><li>Sinfully Spicy suggests <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> crushed kasuri methi (dried fenugreek leaves) for a Punjabi touch.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "More spice, more aroma"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>From Sinfully Spicy’s malai tikka.</li><li><b>Air fryer:</b> <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"200\" data-s=\"0\">200 °C</span> for 16–18 min.</li><li><b>Pan:</b> heat a cast-iron or grill pan over medium-high (not smoking), brush with ghee or butter, cook in one layer 3–4 min, brushing with ghee, then flip and cook until lightly charred.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Pan or air fryer"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Chicken is safe at <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"74\" data-s=\"0\">74 °C</span></b> in the centre.</li><li>Cut the biggest piece open if unsure.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Is it cooked?"
  }
 ],
